    {"id": "cad_03", "condition": "cad_mi", "hop": "chronic_cad", "text": "Chronic Coronary Disease (CCD) per 2023 ACC/AHA: Stable coronary disease includes patients with prior MI, prior revascularization (PCI or CABG), stable angina, or ischemia on stress testing without acute presentation. Diagnostic evaluation includes resting ECG, coronary CT angiography or stress testing (exercise or pharmacologic with imaging), and coronary angiography for high-risk features. Angina classified by Canadian Cardiovascular Society (CCS) Class I to IV based on activity threshold triggering symptoms."},
